Explore the Spookier Side of Space in No Man’s Sky: FORSAKEN!
Last month’s COSMOS update saw a huge uplift in XBOX and Game Pass Travellers old and new journeying to the No Man’s Sky universe to check out the space overhaul which COSMOS ushered in. A whole host of new discoveries appeared in the space between planets, players had the ability to own and customise their own space stations, and much, much more. Today, with the release of our next update, FORSAKEN, we’re staying in space but things have got a whole lot…darker!&nbsp;
As with all our updates, we couldn’t help but squeeze in a few extra features too. With the advent of FORSAKEN, we’ve added a number of lavish new corvette cockpits, seamless warping to the stars you see in the sky, a new minimal HUD mode for advanced players, a radial weapon select, package courier missions, and more!&nbsp;
It’s been a busy year for the No Man’s Sky team, and FORSAKEN is their fifth major update (after REMNANT, XENO ARENA, THE SWARM, and COSMOS). We’re already deep in planning for what sort of craziness we can get up to in 2027.
Vessels of preserved organic matter have begun to appear in deep space, concealed within the nooks and shadows of derelict hulks and infested space outposts. These haunted mementos have attracted a number of enigmatic traders from all corners of the universe, all set upon gathering the samples for their collections.
Fortunately, these strange opportunists are only too pleased to lean on the expertise of experienced Travellers and whoever has mastered the skills of salvaging such in-demand materials. Any brave courier willing to venture into these ominous treasure troves and salvage their curious bounty can barter with forsaken traders, exchanging mementos for unique, sinisterly biomechanical corvette modules. Spook up your existing corvette exterior, or lean fully into the creepy vibe and build a whole new scarecraft.&nbsp;
And the macabre cosmetics aren’t confined purely to your starship. Determined scavengers will be rewarded with the grotesque new larva tank helmet, and may purchase the wriggling larva cannon multi-tool &#8211; for the right quantity of preserved grubs.&nbsp;

All playable from November 3.
PlayStation Plus Monthly Games for November: Dead Island 2, Tomb Raider IV &#8211; VI Remastered, Monster Train 2
Tackle the sun-kissed undead, uncover ancient relics, and jump aboard a train for a deckbuilding journey through Heaven, Hell and beyond. Dead Island 2, Tomb Raider IV &#8211; VI Remastered, Monster Train 2 form your PlayStation Plus Monthly Games for November, with all available to play from Tuesday November 3 to Monday, November 30.&nbsp;
Let’s take a closer look at each of the games.
Dead Island 2 | PS5, PS4&nbsp;
Welcome to HELL-A. The City of Angels has been transformed into a hellish sprawl, its populace now mutated into disgusting zombies with an insatiable appetite for humans. In this extensive, visceral RPG experience you’ll journey to iconic LA locations, taking on quests, meeting eccentric survivors and enjoying a joyously pulpy narrative along the way. The game’s brutal melee combat gives you access to an expansive array of inventive zombie-slaying weaponry that lets you slice, smash and tear through the hordes before they get the chance to do the same to you. Explore the game’s expansive world alone, or practice strength in numbers in online three-player co-op to increase your chances of survival.
This single player deckbuilding roguelite sees you command clans formed of a makeshift alliance between former angels and demons, as they work together to oust powerful beings known as Titans, who have seized control of Heaven. Now, you must command these clans aboard newly forged trains, and embark on your journey through Hell, Heaven, and the Abyss, to defeat the Titans before they destroy this world. Choose from a selection of five brand new clans, each with its own unique strengths and gameplay to forge strategies fitting your personal playstyle. With three vertical levels to defend against dangerous new enemies, you’ll need to recruit powerful new units, upgrade cards, and experiment to survive.&nbsp;
Last chance to add the PlayStation Plus Monthly Games for October
PlayStation Plus members have until Monday November 2 to add the PlayStation Plus Monthly Games for October &#8211;&nbsp;
